<title>BELGIUM: Europe 1996 aluminium output put at 3.18 mln T.</title>
<headline>Europe 1996 aluminium output put at 3.18 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>European production of primary aluminium is forecast rising to 3.18 million tonnes in 1996 from 3.13 million tonnes last year, the European Aluminium Association said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Production totaled 1.86 million tonnes between January and July 1996, up 2.8 percent from a year ago.</p>
<p>The members of European Aluminium Association are Austria, Belgium, Britain, Denmark, Finland, France, Germany, Greece, Italy, Netherlands, Norway, Spain, Sweden, Switzerland and Turkey.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 32 2 287 6830</p>
